{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdvRsj5Hiny8uTGvk3XZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate and it passed the self-check (`OK`). The check doesn't test novelty, convergence or speed, so it's not yet known whether admission will accept it.\n\n**Model name:** `personal_engagement_factor`\n\n**What I refined and what changed:** this refines the incumbent, `personal_pattern_detection_gain`. Everything in it is kept: the personal ideal switching rate with leniency toward over-alternation, the personal weights on imbalance and the longest streak, the shared structural cues scaled by each person's pattern-detection gain, and the personal guessing rate.\n\nThe one change: these traits are no longer independent. Each person has one engagement level that, through fitted weights, sharpens their sensitivity to switching, raises their pattern-detection gain and lowers their guessing rate. So people who follow the majority on one cue tend to follow it on all of them. This targets the critique's one finding that survives the false-discovery-rate correction: people differ in how often they agree with the majority choice more than the incumbent produces (q = 0.048). In the code this adds one shared engagement score per person (`z_eng`) and three weights linking it to the three traits.\n\n**Self-check result:** the 1-chain, 100-draw smoke fit gave ELPD-LOO −3455.3, close to the incumbent's −3451.1. Two caveats about that number:\n- **Reliability:** the check flagged PSIS-LOO as unreliable, with 9.4% of trials having a high Pareto k against a 1% tolerance. That may just reflect the short fit, but it could also mean the full fit's estimate is untrustworthy.\n- **Convergence and speed:** with one chain, R-hat couldn't be computed, so convergence is unchecked. The extra weights could also trade off against each other, which might fail the convergence gate. The smoke fit took 120 s; the full admission fit has a 30-minute limit per sampling run.\n\nThe files are in `.../experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_3/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2699,"cache_read_input_tokens":97843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2699,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d089a69d-9ffc-43ac-9ad2-f47231707b3b","uuid":"3ebde171-e417-43da-9528-633d52d7c3d3","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:57:39.057Z","request_id":"req_011CfdvRsMVoxTqqh46NbtC8"}
